     marks inside inline elements. -->
<rfc number='7002' version='3'>
  <link rel='alternate' href='https://example.invalid/rfc7002'/>
  <front>
    <title>Markup &amp;amp; Entities</title>
  </front>
  <middle>
    <section pn='section-1'>
      <t pn='section-1-1'>A server <!-- a comment --><bcp14>MUST</bcp14> keep &amp;amp; as written<?pi skipped?>, decode &#65;&#x42;&#x43; and &lt;x&gt;<![CDATA[ MUST]]> once.</t>
      <t pn='section-1-2'>A client <em><bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14></em> see <xref target='r' format='default' derivedContent='say "R"'/> as &apos;data&apos;.</t>
      <t pn='section-1-3'>A sender <bcp14>MUST <em>NOT</em></bcp14> split, and a proxy <bcp14>SHALL</bcp14> wait.</t>
      <t pn='section-1-4'>See <xref target='r' format='none' derivedContent=''>a server <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> retry</xref>. Nothing else is said.</t>
    </section>
  </middle>
  <back>
